WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:38.740
Happy New Year!

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:50.210
Tanaka, that was a good idea to go on a sunrise cruise.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.250
Yes.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:56.300
Everyone, when the sun emerges from the horizon, we'll celebrate with this.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:06.060
You can't! The noisemaker will scare the sun, and it'll go back into hiding!

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:10.520
I don't think that will happen.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.150
Don't worry, Cream.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.280
The sun will enjoy it too.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:20.280
Oh really? Then let me have one too.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.080
All that's left is Sonic.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.120
Huh?

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.290
Look up.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.210
Episode 40

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.210
Eggman Company

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.440
You should've come too.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.400
No way! I don't want to get sunburned!

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.950
That will ruin my skin.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.910
Just rub on some suntan oil.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:07.750
Suntan oil isn't enough to protect my sensitive skin.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:14.090
Just admit that you feel uncomfortable in the bright sunlight because you're a thief.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:21.470
Everyone, it's almost time!

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.600
Are you ready?

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.480
When I give the signal, set off the noisemaker.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.520
"Go!" will be the signal.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.980
It's almost time.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.970
What's happening?

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.430
I told you this would happen.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.060
An eclipse?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.390
Why is there suddenly an eclipse?

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.730
It's the Egg Moon.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.730
Contact the President!

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.980
Right!

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.450
What is it?

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:29.660
The Egg Moon suddenly changed its orbit and blocked the sun.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.330
What? Is this Eggman's fault again?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.460
Hello, everybody!

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.590
Eggman!

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.130
Mr. President, long time no see!

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.840
Eggman has infiltrated the President's office!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.470
There's a misunderstanding!

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.680
Wait!! Let's hear him out.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:57.730
No wonder you're the President. You're very understanding.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.070
What's the misunderstanding?

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:04.360
Egg Moon left its orbit due to an accident.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:11.580
I think there was a magnetic anomaly that affected the Egg Moon.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.000
Is that true?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.660
Why would I lie to you?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:19.590
Believe me! I've changed!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.920
I'd like to trust you, but...

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:26.630
I'll take full responsibility for what happened!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.590
So please believe me!

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.640
Mr. President!

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.230
I'll trust you.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.780
Thank you, Mr. President!

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.360
Thank you, my friend!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:01.000
My vacation is a waste!

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.210
Getting angry isn't good for your skin.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.260
A world with eternal night is perfect for me!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.050
You'll get used to it quickly.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.810
It feels so good!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:26.360
We didn't use the noisemaker, but the sun still disappeared!

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.240
It didn't disappear.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:32.280
It's just hiding because it's shy.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.670
What's your plan?

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.840
Are you going to move Egg Moon by remote control?

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.930
That's not possible.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:58.810
The receiver seems to be broken, so I can't move it from here.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.310
Does that mean that the eclipse will continue?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.690
It'll take time to repair the Egg Moon.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.150
First, I have to find the cause of the problem.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:14.030
It'll take six months... Actually, it'll take at least a year.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.870
You must be kidding! We can't wait that long!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.790
Of course not!

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:24.040
Therefore, in the meantime, we'll have to provide sunlight to Earth using a different method.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.960
What's the different method?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.760
You'll have to wait and see.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.300
It'll surprise you.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.100
Preparations are complete!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:37.970
Complete!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.600
We're ready to begin at anytime.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.770
Okay!

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.150
Wait, Decoe and Bocoe!

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.230
Show some respect when you talk to us!

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:49.780
That's not important. I have a message for you from Dr. Eggman.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.530
Start the plan!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.910
Yeah!

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.870
That's it?

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.580
What about my role?

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.240
Oh yeah.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.580
This robot will automatically start playing the three-stringed Japanese guitar.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.420
All right! Leave it to me!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.670
You're pretty good.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.470
You're great.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.680
It stirs the soul.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.940
Thank you for listening.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.690
I wish others could have heard it.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:32.360
I didn't know Messenger Robo had that hidden talent.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.860
We also have to step up!

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.820
What can we do?

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.950
Our hidden talent will be to speak in Chinese!

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.330
That's a great idea!

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:44.870
Wu! (Five)

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.000
Si! (Four)

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:46.920
San! (Three)

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:47.960
Yan! (Two)

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:49.250
Yi! (One)

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.800
Game over!

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:17.740
Stop!

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.240
Opening light reflector.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.420
Alter angle by 30 degrees.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.940
10%.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.360
20%.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.150
30%.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:22.720
Since the sun is blocked, there continues to be no sunlight.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.890
However, the sunlight recharging plan is progressing thanks to the newly-reformed Eggman.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.900
We're interrupting this program for a commercial.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:38.990
Eggman Company TV Shopping!

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:45.580
To supply your household with sunlight, you need a special device.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.200
This is the device.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.750
Ta-daa!

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:57.090
This is called the Sunshine Ball. Just one will provide your household with sunshine.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:07.470
During our apology sale, rental and installation fees are half price!

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:13.310
I want to offer it for free, but there are maintenance costs. I'm sorry.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.110
Don't let this opportunity pass you by!

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:20.740
Hurry and call Eggman Company to order!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.500
What should we do?

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.300
Hmm...

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.340
Without sunshine, I can't hang the clothes out to dry.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:44.090
That device would be nice to have.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.350
I agree.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.310
I'll give them a call.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.270
Sonic!

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.820
Eggman is behind this.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.650
Sonic won't accept it.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:03.820
Or more accurately, he gets on his nerves.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.320
Really?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.830
But I thought they made peace.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.250
Not completely.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.410
After all, they're eternal rivals.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.120
I see...

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:28.220
You may have difficulty getting through, but don't worry, because we have plenty in stock!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.510
Installation complete!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.260
Let's turn it on.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.900
It's so warm.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.860
The light is exactly the same as sunlight.

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.570
You're right.

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:37.790
Eggman Company is doing well.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.590
However...

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:54.730
Thank you very much.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:58.770
If you're happy, that makes us happy too!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:01.400
We're glad to be of help.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:08.030
Thank you.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.530
Thanks!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:16.540
I never knew that doing good deeds would make me feel this great!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.500
You can say that again!

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:29.130
So you're saying that the rich can have light, but the poor can't?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:31.930
No, that's not my intention.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:34.720
All citizens should be treated fairly!

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.930
Provide sunlight to all the citizens!

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.520
That's right!

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.440
What do you want the city to do?

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:46.230
Station Square must sign a contract with Eggman Company!

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:54.870
I vote yes! There will be discounts, and it will help the masses!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:59.330
I vote no! How will you explain this to the people who already signed contracts?

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:02.420
Order!

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.420
Hello!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.800
Station Square?

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.510
Your order is confirmed. Thank you!

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.010
Dr. Eggman!

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:15.970
Call me president!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.020
President Eggman!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:24.150
President! President! President Eggman!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.690
At this rate, we'll have our stock listed soon.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:31.110
Since we have more subscribers than we anticipated, we'll have to build more Mirror Towers.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.490
You're right, president!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.000
This is the President.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.710
It's me, Dr. Eggman.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.500
I want to build more Mirror Towers.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:49.090
Can you provide me with some government-owned land?

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.970
Of course!

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:53.510
Thank you!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:16:01.640
No, Dr. Eggman. I should be thanking you!

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:04.520
Not just me, but everyone in the country!

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.860
Is that right?

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.290
This really is the sun.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.450
I feel thankful.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:23.500
It's just like the real sun.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:33.180
You're a hero who not only saved our country, but the entire Earth!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.970
A hero? Just like Sonic?

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.140
Of course!

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:46.270
Does that mean that I'm now the main character of this cartoon?

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:52.650
Hello?

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.740
Dr. Eggman?

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.870
Eggman is getting carried away.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.090
I've had enough of them!

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.350
There you go.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.270
You should add a little more soil.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:24.060
Okay.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.680
I agree.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.400
What happened? The light suddenly turned off.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:39.870
What's going on?

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:43.500
This is so irritating.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:47.080
Why did this happen so suddenly?

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:55.590
This is an emergency report from Eggman Company.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.720
Why did the Sunshine Balls turn off?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:02.600
This incident occurred because Mirror Tower #18 collapsed.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:08.650
We're rebuilding as fast as we can, so we should have the lights restored by the evening.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:11.060
What caused the tower to collapse?

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:13.610
We're still investigating.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:15.320
It can't be...

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.570
It can't be what?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.570
It's nothing.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.370
It can't be.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.790
But where did Sonic go?

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.040
No way!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.550
This must be a mistake!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:42.220
There's no mistake. Please take a good look at this.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.560
Sonic, why?

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.020
I can't believe it.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:52.020
Sonic was always our ally!

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:58.700
From Sonic's point-of-view, I don't think he ever thought he was your ally.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.360
What do you mean by that?

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:04.530
Sonic just does what he likes.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:08.040
It just so happened that his interests matched up with yours.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.420
But this time, they don't.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:12.790
Interests?

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:17.130
Is he upset that we teamed up with Eggman?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.340
Beats me.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.630
What should we do, Mr. President?

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.640
Should we release this image to the public?

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.190
What is it? We're in the middle of a meeting.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:37.110
Mr. President, big trouble! Another Mirror Tower has been destroyed!

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:38.740
What?

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:44.700
Mr. President, please make a decision.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:49.040
Release the image.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:05.600
It has been confirmed that Sonic the Hedgehog destroyed the Mirror Tower!

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.430
What?

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:13.810
It's a lie! Sonic would never do something like that!

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.730
It has to be a mistake!

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.730
Chris! Mr. Thorndyke! Big trouble!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.190
What's wrong?

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:24.660
Where's Sonic? Bring Sonic out!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.200
We know you're here!

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.910
Hand over Sonic!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:34.040
This is spiraling out of control.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.580
Why would Sonic do that?

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.380
Sonic must have something in mind.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:46.340
Are you saying that he's upset because everyone's happy with Eggman?

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.760
No, I think it's something else.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.720
What else could it be?

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.980
I don't know either!

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.730
Oh no!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.070
I'll pound 'em all away!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:03.110
You can't! They'll think you're the enemy too!

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.490
But we can't leave things as is!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.410
